><< stidi zo xomoi .i mu'a cusku lu le xomoi to beti toi cu broda
>  li'u (Maybe: "Which-th" as in "Which-th (of these), is (something)?")
>   >>
>Remind me what is wrong with {mo} here, except it forces left grouping when
>you might want something rightward.

The classic argument against "mo" has been that it is too vague and 
practically invites irrelevancy.  It is saying "supply me a selbri here", 
which in the case of "le mo broda" is asking only for a modifier - it is 
not necessarily asking for a clarifier.

